<title>USA: Pease Oil sells convertible debentures.</title>
<headline>Pease Oil sells convertible debentures.</headline>
<dateline>GRAND JUNCTION, Colo. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pease Oil and Gas Co said Wednesday it privately placed $5.0 million of 10 percent collateralized convertible debentures.</p>
<p>The debentures are convertible into common stock at $3.00 per share and have detachable $1.25 stock purchase warrants.</p>
<p>Pease said its proceeds were used in part to pay off the entire balance of the outstanding debt with Colorado National Bank.  The rest will provide funds to pursue additional drilling and development activities.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
